# Rasterizer comparison

Question: How do the named tools render the same static TTF and paragraph in monochrome?

Use the original tool rasterization paths; compose exported glyphs only by their native advances and bearings. Shared inputs are a fully instantiated Roboto Regular, explicit three-line text, equal pixels per em, integer origin and baselines, black on white, no antialiasing, and disabled kerning where possible. Preserve native glyph and text metrics. Keep output differences as pending optical assessment, with no quality ranking. Capture native-color output before any composition. Do not threshold or redraw another tool and label it as the requested tool. Where an adapter or sizing change is necessary, record it. Windows GDI requires a genuine Windows runtime and must be marked unavailable if no Windows host is accessible.

Sources: ImageMagick text rendering https://usage.imagemagick.org/text/ ; LVGL converter https://github.com/lvgl/lv_font_conv ; Adafruit converter https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit-GFX-Library/blob/master/fontconvert/fontconvert.c ; truetype2gfx https://rop.nl/truetype2gfx/ ; FontForge display https://fontforge.org/docs/ui/dialogs/display.html ; Core Graphics https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcontext/setshouldantialias(_:) ; GDI https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/wingdi/nf-wingdi-createfonta ; repository tools/generator/API.md and docs/revisions/001/README.md.

Decision boundary: successfully produced, binary, unclipped, reproducible images with true engine provenance. Mechanical verification does not establish optical acceptance. All work stays in this ignored run folder; no changes to preview selections or source.
