# Roboto 16 px rasterizer comparison

Six monochrome paragraph images are generated from one static Roboto Regular instance at exactly 16 pixels per em. Open `index.html` through the local server for aligned native, 2× and 4× views. Each card links its original PNG; `display/` contains identical common crops with empty margins removed.

| Result | Actual rendering path | Adaptation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ImageMagick | Installed ImageMagick 7.1.2-30, FreeType delegate, antialiasing disabled | Direct text drawing at explicit baselines |
| LVGL converter | Pinned `lv_font_conv@1.5.3`, bundled FreeType WASM, 1 bpp | Compose exported glyph pixels using converter metrics; half-up advance quantization matches its published C writer. This does not claim LVGL widget-layout parity. |
| Adafruit GFX | Pinned upstream fontconvert commit `1cb8122cec6c57f026985ec4a44164cd3624f406`, FreeType 2.14.3, native mono and interpreter v35 | Replace point/DPI size request with exact 16-pixel size request; compose using exported GFX offsets and advances. Not an online-site capture. |
| FontForge native | FontForge 20251009 release, existing native `SplineFontRasterize` implementation | Isolated headless build; one-line dispatch change selects the existing native renderer instead of FreeType. Compose its 1-bit BDF pixels and DWIDTH metrics. |
| Apple CoreText | CoreText/CoreGraphics on this macOS host | Antialiasing, smoothing, subpixel positioning and ligatures disabled; direct text drawing with the supplied font |
| Glypherie | Current working repository source and documented working preview | `font_hints_auto` + `free_type_mono_terminals`, diagonal fitting on; maintained surface API, zero uniform tracking. A separately labelled legacy baseline is retained under `repo/output/`. |

## Shared input

The repository's `fonts/Roboto.ttf` is instantiated at `wght=400`, `wdth=100` with fontTools 4.60.1. Every renderer consumes the resulting identical static `inputs/Roboto-Regular.ttf`. No tool receives an alternative font or a fallback face.

- Original source SHA-256: `d7598e12c5dbef095ff8272cfc55da0250bd07fbdecbac8a530b9b277872a134`.
- Shared static SHA-256: `c76bbfa0c89791a8f3c6c25c5676ff3cc4a65833e521898127396c9c1ffe850a`.
- Exact text and hash: `inputs/text.txt` and `inputs/font.json`.
- Output: 1200×176 pixels, black on white, x origin 16, baselines y=40/88/136; 16 px only. Pair kerning disabled; each path retains its declared native advance policy, so this is a comparison of rendered text including placement.

> Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs.  
> The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.  
> Minimum effort, maximum clarity: AVATAR To Wa 0123456789.

## Verification

Muse generated the external and repository adapters and independently reviewed their output and provenance. Its report is `verification/report.json`; parent verification is `parent-final-check.json`.

Parent checks confirm all six original images have exactly the black/white levels {0,255}, the shared dimensions, real ink, and no ink touching a canvas edge. Each displayed crop equals the corresponding original pixels exactly. LVGL and Adafruit raw exports and composed PNGs reproduce identically. ImageMagick and CoreText reproduce identically; the repository source remained unchanged across a locked offline build and two identical captures (`inputs/repo-source-snapshot.json`). FontForge retains native BDF and PNG determinism evidence in its provenance files.

The verified LVGL adapter rounding defect was corrected to match JavaScript `Math.round` before delivery. Native glyph pixels were not modified. Source, settings, commands, raw exports, patches, versions and hashes are retained beside each output. FontForge's source identity is its pinned release archive and archive hash; its build banner can inherit this enclosing repository's Git ID and is not an upstream FontForge commit identifier.

The repository source was already dirty and received concurrent edits during the task; the final capture records a stable source snapshot rather than pretending the image represents clean HEAD. This task's maintained-source and publication selections were not edited. All task artifacts are under this Git-ignored run folder.

## Limits and assessment

- Windows GDI: no native Windows executor is available. VMware Fusion is installed, but `vmrun list` reports zero running VMs. No substituted GDI image is claimed.
- truetype2gfx online preview: the published source at commit `5e38d5d80a8f45fad03139c6dfb3ca287b95113e` draws antialiased PHP GD text on a 320×240 canvas. It does not display the exported Adafruit monochrome bitmap. The local Adafruit conversion result is labelled separately; no thresholded website preview is presented as native monochrome output. Evidence is `online/metadata.json` and the pinned source checkout.
- Output differences remain pending optical assessment. These mechanical checks establish comparable inputs, preserved output and reproducibility; they do not rank readability or rendering quality.
.landing {
  color: var(--studio-foreground);
  background: var(--studio-surface);
  min-height: 100%;
}

.landing__main {
  width: min(1160px, calc(100% - 64px));
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 100px) 64px;
}

.landing__hero {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
  align-items: center;
  gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px);
}

.landing__eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 20px;
  color: var(--studio-heading);
  font-family: var(--font-studio);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: .1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.landing h1, .landing h2, .landing h3 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
}

.landing h1 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: clamp(42px, 5.5vw, 68px);
  line-height: 1.05;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -.055em;
}

.landing h1 span {
  color: var(--studio-heading);
}

.landing__intro {
  max-width: 440px;
  margin: 24px 0 28px;
  color: var(--studio-muted);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.landing__actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 20px;
}

.landing__actions [data-slot="button"] {
  background: var(--studio-foreground);
  color: var(--studio-surface);
  text-decoration: none;
}

.landing__actions [data-slot="button"]:hover {
  opacity: .85;
}

.landing__text-link {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
